      "content": "Apologies for the confusion. To file a formal report with your local council about the flickering streetlamp, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. Find your local council's contact information, which is usually available on their official website or by searching for your area online.\n2. Look for a section on the website dedicated to reporting issues, such as \"report a problem\" or \"report an incident.\"\n3. Fill out the necessary form, providing details such as the exact location of the streetlamp, the nature of the problem, and the time it occurs.\n4. Some councils may also offer a dedicated phone line or email address for reporting issues. If so, you can use these methods to submit your report.\n5. After submitting the report, you should receive a confirmation, which may include a reference number. Keep this for your records.\n6. The council will typically assign a work order number to your report, which you can use to track the progress of the repair.\n\nThe time it takes to fix the streetlamp can vary depending on the council's workload and the complexity of the repair. However, it usually takes a few days to a week for a repairman to arrive and fix the issue. If the problem persists, you can",
